{"name":"Timeless Seafoam","hex":"#afe4e2","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"timeless","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Eternal.","Not affected by time; ageless."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A gene encoding an essential protein that regulates circadian rhythm, normally written in italics: timeless."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/timeless"},{"term":"seafoam","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A foam created by the agitation of seawater.","A light green-blue color."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seafoam"}],"entries":[{"title":"Sea foam","blocks":[{"text":"Sea foam, ocean foam, beach foam, or spume is a type of foam created by the agitation of seawater, particularly when it contains higher concentrations of dissolved organic matter derived from sources such as the offshore breakdown of algal blooms. These compounds can act as surfactants or foaming agents. As the seawater is churned by breaking waves in the surf zone adjacent to the shore, the surfactants under these turbulent conditions trap air, forming persistent bubbles that stick to each other through surface tension."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Sea_foam_at_Ocean_Beach_in_San_Francisco_-1_on_3-25-11.jpg/330px-Sea_foam_at_Ocean_Beach_in_San_Francisco_-1_on_3-25-11.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea_foam"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Sea_spray_sea_foam_connection.png/500px-Sea_spray_sea_foam_connection.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Sea_spray_sea_foam_connection.png/1280px-Sea_spray_sea_foam_connection.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/85/Sea_spray_sea_foam_connection.png/500px-Sea_spray_sea_foam_connection.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Connection between sea foam and sea spray formation. The dark orange line indicates processes common to the formation of both sea spray and sea foam.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASea_spray_sea_foam_connection.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Brandung_%28MW_2015.02.27.%29.JPG/500px-Brandung_%28MW_2015.02.27.%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Brandung_%28MW_2015.02.27.%29.JPG/1280px-Brandung_%28MW_2015.02.27.%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Brandung_%28MW_2015.02.27.%29.JPG/500px-Brandung_%28MW_2015.02.27.%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sea foam usually contains a mixture of decomposed organic materials","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrandung_(MW_2015.02.27.).JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Plankton_creates_sea_foam_2.jpg/500px-Plankton_creates_sea_foam_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Plankton_creates_sea_foam_2.jpg/1280px-Plankton_creates_sea_foam_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Plankton_creates_sea_foam_2.jpg/500px-Plankton_creates_sea_foam_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":" Bubbles of plankton-enriched foam left in a tide pool after high tide","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APlankton_creates_sea_foam_2.jpg"}],"sounds":{"timeless":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","s